---
id: misra-chaapu-korvai-1
name: Misra Chaapu korvai
counts: 7/2
shape: down
nadai: any
ticks: "0 1/7 3/7 5/7"
role: korvai
source: >-
  karya, Solkattu/Score/Mridangam2018.hs, tir_18_06_15, learned from Ganesh,
  2018-06-15 (github.com/elaforge/karya, GPL-3.0, used with permission). A
  tirmanam written there as tri (od.__) (t.k.o.o.k.o.o.k): the phrase three
  times, joined by thom with din. It fills one cycle and resolves on the next
  sam. Converted as ta, thi for ki, thom, and "thom+dhin". Unverified by a
  player.
accents:
  0: 1.1
---
\cycle("|7|")
\beatDuration(4)
mrid: ta thi thom thom
      thi thom thom thi
      "thom+dhin" , ta thi
      thom thom thi thom
      thom thi "thom+dhin" ,
      ta thi thom thom
      thi thom thom thi
